            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 39,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm pretty confused here.....  \"only a few\" would imply that we only partially read the config file?  I don't see how that's possible in the code."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 39,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Comment made by mistake.  I think I have line of sight on why this was happening."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Interesting, so this bug will pop up if you don't call requestRoutesManager:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/0c814aa604b36cff01b495f9c335f981c7be83be/redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp#L577\n\nWhich incidentally instantiates the config.  If that's disabled for some reason, the config won't get initted because there's nothing else that \"needs\" it if you do basic auth.\n\nCould we be explicit about initing it and move the getConfig() call into webserver_run.cpp?\n\nOr alternatively deprecate the EventServiceStore class entirely, but I'm willing to accept this as-is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Right. it is currently incidentally loaded by requestRoutesManager().\ngetConfig() is better to load explicitly and I changed to do it in webserver_run.cpp as suggested.\n\nOne key cause is at https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/0c814aa604b36cff01b495f9c335f981c7be83be/include/persistent_data.hpp#L184\n\nI add the detail into the commit message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/event_service_manager.hpp",
                    "line": 103,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Would really like to see EventServiceStore just go away.  There's really no reason for it to exist anymore now that it's backed by the main config.\n\nThis works, but please consider the cleanup."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/event_service_manager.hpp",
                    "line": 103,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's consider EventServiceStore deprecation separately."
                }
            ],
